Linda; 
From what I read the climate has been changing for billions of years and I expect it to keep changing for billions of years after the last humans are long gone and I do not think any little adjustments will change that. 
People need to accept the fact that we are temporary inhabitants here on earth and enjoy it while we are here.

You appear not to understand genocide.  Here is Article 2 of the convention that succinctly defines genocide.

Article 2 of the Convention defines genocide as

...any of the following acts committed with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group, as such:

(a) Killing members of the group;
(b) Causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group;
(c) Deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part;
(d) Imposing measures intended to prevent births within the group;
(e) Forcibly transferring children of the group to another group.
— Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide, Article 2

From this definition, what was done in the schools clearly fits all five of the conditions when only one condition needs to be met.

Canada meets all five of these conditions today in their dealings with Indigenous People. Fact.

